<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nizari Ismaili state</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nizari Ismaili</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizari</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> state was a network of mountain fortresses in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> governed by the Nizari branch of Ismaili <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiism">Shi'ism</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alamut">Alamut</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a> mountains from the late eleventh century. It resisted larger powers for over a century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> destroyed it in 1256 by capturing Alamut, before advancing on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state.jpg" alt="Nizari Ismaili state" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jolle · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alamut.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
